18
00:01:21,130 --> 00:01:25,090
Well, I believe the answer lies in a combination of all of these elements.

19
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:32,430
Our campaign will really hammer home the point that the X420 is a state-of-the-art laptop for all of your computing needs.

20
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:36,430
With our television campaign, we hope to really reach out to a huge audience.

21
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:41,730
We have a great ad campaign planned, focused on the fantastic USPs of the X420.

22
00:01:42,530 --> 00:01:51,030
We've hired one of the best PR companies to work with us on the campaign and have already completed three separate TV adverts, all focusing on one key feature of the X420.

23
00:01:51,870 --> 00:01:56,730
I'm excited to say that today for the first time we will unveil to all of you here the first of these advertisements.

24
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:14,960
All right, we're back and now let's take a look at five key words on Language Takeaway.

25
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:15,400
Language Takeaway.

26
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:20,680
All right, so first up, Marco, we have a verb.

27
00:02:20,690 --> 00:02:21,890
The verb is to devise.

28
00:02:22,870 --> 00:02:25,410
That's right, so we devised a campaign.

29
00:02:26,450 --> 00:02:31,690
Okay, so to devise in this case means to create or to come up with.

30
00:02:31,990 --> 00:02:32,470
That's right.

31
00:02:32,930 --> 00:02:40,890
I think in many movies you will hear that someone will devise a plan to destroy the world for example.

32
00:02:41,090 --> 00:02:42,930
Right, or to devise a scheme.

33
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:49,630
So that's to create or to come up with a plan or come up with something.

34
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:59,370
And talking about the computers, he mentioned a couple of words that describe it, especially the affordability of the laptop computer.

35
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:08,260
Okay, so yeah, there's this string of nouns that Mr. Ford thinks are very important relating to the perfect laptop.

36
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:11,640
And in this case, affordability is the first one.

37
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:15,620
So something that is affordable is something that you can have the money to buy.

38
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:16,840
It's not too expensive.

39
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:18,660
That's the adjective affordable.

40
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:22,080
Affordability means whether or not something is expensive.

41
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:23,160
That's right.

42
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:29,880
So if you think of the adjective affordable, the noun would be affordability.

43
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:34,920
So this is just the way that you can transform an adjective into a noun.

44
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:39,200
Right, so this is something that comes up a lot when we're talking about buying things.

45
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:43,980
For example, Marco, I could say, what do you look for when you're buying a car?

46
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:45,720
Right, so I can say affordability.

47
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:51,160
And you could also say our next one, which is reliability.

48
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:51,370
That's right.

49
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:55,690
So if you look for a car, you are also looking for reliability.

50
00:03:56,660 --> 00:03:58,550
And this comes from the adjective reliable.

51
00:03:59,250 --> 00:04:02,970
All right, so something is reliable if you can depend on it.

52
00:04:03,370 --> 00:04:07,810
It means, you know, in the case of a laptop or a car, it won't break easily.

53
00:04:08,190 --> 00:04:08,710
That's right.

54
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:12,000
Or a person can also be reliable.

55
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,490
You can trust that person to help you, for example.

56
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:19,200
Or I can trust that he'll never be late or never forget that we have an appointment.

57
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:20,820
That's exactly right.

58
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:34,580
Well, moving on to the next part of Mr. Ford's speech, he talked about the television campaign and how he really hopes to reach out to a huge audience with this television advert.

59
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:41,120
All right, so the reason we've chosen this is because it's important to remember this as a phrase to reach out to.

60
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,080
That means to connect with.

61
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:50,000
And I think your example of television is a really great one because television allows people to reach out to many, many, many people.

62
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:50,700
That's right.

63
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:57,580
Also, for example, with Internet, you are able to reach out to many people all over the world.

64
00:04:58,020 --> 00:05:00,720
So, to reach out to is to connect with.

65
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:01,700
Okay.

66
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:12,760
And for our last word, when he was about to show everyone the TV advert, he said that tonight for the first time we will unveil the first of these advertisements.

67
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:13,540
All right.

68
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:20,260
So, to unveil something is actually very exciting because to unveil something is to show it for the very first time.

69
00:05:20,540 --> 00:05:21,080
That's right.

70
00:05:21,260 --> 00:05:26,520
So, maybe you've seen in car shows where they have a car under a big white sheet.

71
00:05:26,990 --> 00:05:31,890
And on that night, they're going to unveil the new model of the, I don't know, the Ford car.

72
00:05:32,630 --> 00:05:36,230
So, that's what it means, to unveil, to take away this veil and show everyone.

73
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:37,390
To unveil.

74
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:39,040
All right.

75
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:40,160
So, a lot of good key words there.

