94
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:34,530
Fluency Builder

95
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:48,410
So in the beginning, Mr. Ford is talking about this exciting X420 and he says that, you know, he would like to say that without the help of each and every one of you, the campaign could not have been created.

96
00:07:48,730 --> 00:07:50,930
So each and every one of you.

97
00:07:51,290 --> 00:07:51,650
That's right.

98
00:07:51,830 --> 00:07:57,670
This is just a phrase where you emphasize that everyone helped you or that you are thanking everyone.

99
00:07:58,010 --> 00:08:02,210
So in a speech, you can say, I want to thank each and every one of you.

100
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:05,800
So I want to thank everyone is basically what you're saying.

101
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:10,470
And it's, it's interesting because it's kind of like you're saying every single person was important.

102
00:08:10,940 --> 00:08:11,940
Right.

103
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:13,800
So it's not just like, Hey guys, thank you.

104
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:14,990
It's like, no, thank you.

105
00:08:15,320 --> 00:08:16,430
And you and you and you.

106
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:20,950
So each and every one of you, it really emphasizes that each person has helped.

107
00:08:21,210 --> 00:08:21,610
That's right.

108
00:08:21,910 --> 00:08:27,010
And it's a really nice way of, for example, thanking someone saying, I want to thank each and every one of you.

109
00:08:27,110 --> 00:08:28,290
It sounds a lot more personal.

110
00:08:28,490 --> 00:08:28,730
Definitely.

111
00:08:29,960 --> 00:08:30,960
Okay.

112
00:08:30,960 --> 00:08:40,060
And he also used another very interesting phrase when he said, I'd like to take my hat off and really thank you all for your wonderful work.

113
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:50,180
So this makes me think of a person actually back when people used to wear hats every day, taking his hat off and maybe bowing.

114
00:08:51,140 --> 00:08:57,880
This is something that used to be very polite because you know, when you meet someone or you want to thank someone, you take your hat off as a sign of respect.

115
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:02,040
Well we don't wear hats anymore, so it seems a little funny, but we still say this.

116
00:09:02,380 --> 00:09:03,980
I want to take my hat off to Marco.

117
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:05,060
That means I want to thank you.

118
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:05,600
That's right.

119
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:10,280
So you're showing respect and you're also showing admiration maybe for someone.

120
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:19,060
So maybe if you meet somebody who saved someone's life, you would say, I really want to take my hat off and thank you for the work that you've done.

121
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:19,500
Yes.

122
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:20,160
You're impressed.

123
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:24,720
You respect that person who saved that life and you want to thank them for their good deed.

124
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:25,640
That's right.

125
00:09:26,280 --> 00:09:37,320
Well, moving on, when he continued to talk about Alpha Computers and the marketing efforts, he said, there's no doubt in my mind that we have a great workforce.

126
00:09:38,140 --> 00:09:38,440
All right.

127
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:42,540
So another way to say this is, I definitely think we have a great workforce.

128
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:43,560
That's right.

129
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:45,200
You know, maybe not.

130
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:46,650
It's not as interesting, right?

131
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:59,650
So we're making this more interesting by using a very colorful phrase and to say, there's no doubt that you're a great workforce is good, but there's no doubt in my mind means there's absolutely no way that I could doubt this.

132
00:09:59,970 --> 00:10:02,010
I absolutely believe that you are the best workforce.

133
00:10:02,650 --> 00:10:02,910
Right.

134
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:05,440
So, and you can use it with anything.

135
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:13,000
You can say, there's no doubt in my mind, IBM computers are the best computers out there, for example.

136
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:18,060
Or there's no doubt in my mind that the Yankees will win the World Series next year.

137
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:18,700
That's right.

138
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:20,440
Okay.

139
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:21,200
So that's the way that you can use it.

140
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:24,680
You're basically telling people that you are very, very sure.

141
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:27,700
And what about our last phrase?

142
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:33,600
The very interesting one when he says, our campaign will really hammer home the point.

143
00:10:33,810 --> 00:10:35,190
Okay, well, you can make a point.

144
00:10:35,370 --> 00:10:40,730
You can say, listen, our computers are state of the art and they're the best for your needs.

145
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:50,320
But to hammer home the point means to really emphasize this one important point and to say, listen, you will never forget this.

146
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:51,320
Okay.

147
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:52,250
You will not forget what I'm going to say to you.

148
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:56,380
So you really emphasize it and restate it.

149
00:10:56,380 --> 00:11:03,050
This is something that can be frustrating when you're a consumer, when you're watching an advertisement because you hear them say, this is the best product.

150
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:04,290
You shouldn't buy other products.

151
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:05,880
This is the best product.

152
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:07,400
And they're hammering home the point.

153
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:08,310
They're repeating this message.

154
00:11:08,530 --> 00:11:08,970
That's right.

155
00:11:09,490 --> 00:11:14,060
So it's a colloquial phrase that you can use to really, again, put your point across.

156
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:15,800
Okay.

